{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And I stayed on the mountain</b> — according to the opinion of our Sages (Seder Olam 6), he says that he stayed on the mountain when he went up there with the two tablets in his hand, like the first days of the first tablets — forty days and forty nights. And YHWH listened to me also at that third time, for YHWH passed before his face and YHWH proclaimed: YHWH, YHWH, El, merciful, etc. (Exodus 34:6), and he requested of Him (ibid. 9): and pardon our iniquity and our sin, and take us for an inheritance, and He answered and said: Arise, go, journey before the people, and they shall come and inherit the land. And this is: And let all the people who are among you see the work of YHWH, for it is awesome, that which I am doing with you (ibid. 10)." "And the sense of <b>YHWH was unwilling to destroy you</b> — that He did not want it to be that you would not come and inherit the land, in the same sense as: and they will add still to leave him in the wilderness, and you will destroy all this people (Numbers 32:15). And by way of truth, He did not want destruction to come from Him — that His great Name not be with you. And I have already hinted at this matter in the portion of Ki Tissa."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {0 "Ramban quotes Exodus 34:9 with the phrase וּנְחַלְתָּנוּ ('and take us for an inheritance'), whereas the standard Masoretic text of Exodus 34:9 reads וּנְחַלְתָּנוּ with the same consonants but is typically vocalized as 'and make us an inheritance'; the translation reflects the text as Ramban cites it."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:47:33.232362042Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}